This folder is Delirium Physics 0.9.3 (PVCPC), the engine crate (delirium), its data crate
(delirium-data) and its SDK crate (delirium-sdk: its source and manifest), copied from https://github.com/PVCPC/delirium-physics, commit
23aea85bc761c11b6d3798725ef42364e31ffeb4. nv-rs's crates/delirium-bridge runs it behind New
Physics. Changed: each Cargo.toml's workspace fields written out (version, edition, licence,
publish), and a first line saying so; the engine crate's examples folder left out; the data
crate's five maps kept as hex text and written back by a build.rs, which kv.rs includes (its
first line says so); the SDK built as an rlib only. Nothing else.

Credits: Delirium Physics is written by PVCPC, a Rust port of the Euphoria active ragdoll as
GTA IV has it. Its own credits are in CREDITS.md beside this file (they name the assets of its
Playroom, which nv-rs does not include).

Delirium reads its numbers and its character from the player's own copy of GTA IV at run time
(the program unlocks them). No GTA IV file, and nothing read from one, is in this repository or
in any nv-rs package.

